# With an `or`, the `and` fix would regroup the conditions: not machine-applicable (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
T | where a or b, c
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..20
  PIPELINE@0..19
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "T"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..19
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..16
        NAME_REF@10..11
          IDENT@10..11 "a"
        WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
        OR_KW@12..14 "or"
        WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
        NAME_REF@15..16
          IDENT@15..16 "b"
      COMMA@16..17 ","
      WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
      NAME_REF@18..19
        IDENT@18..19 "c"
  WHITESPACE@19..20 "\n"

error[DS0115]: `where` takes one condition
  --> query:1:17
  |
1 | T | where a or b, c
  |                 ^ a comma does not join conditions
  |
  = help: combine the conditions with `and`: `a or b and c`
